# Railway injects DATABASE_URL automatically when you attach its Postgres
# plugin to this service, and PORT automatically for every service. You only
# need to set this one yourself:
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32

# For local development only (Railway sets these for you in production):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost/terminal_messenger
# PORT=8787

# STUN_PORT is the UDP port for this server's own STUN binding responder
# (see server/src/stun.ts). Defaults to 3478 if unset. Only reachable if
# your deployment exposes a public UDP port — see README's Railway
# deploy section for why that's not true on Railway by default.
# STUN_PORT=3478
